CRITICAL SECURITY REQUIREMENT — AUTHENTICATION AND AUTOMATIC LOGIN

Do not allow automatic login to bypass authentication, device verification, session validation, account status, or server-side authorization.

Incorrect passwords must always fail authentication.

Remember Me may only use securely stored, revocable authentication tokens.

Never store plaintext passwords or expose authentication tokens.

A new or unrecognized device must follow the configured verification policy.

Provide secure logout, logout-all-devices, session expiry, token revocation, password reset and MFA.

Password changes, suspected account compromise and Owner-initiated security actions must revoke affected sessions according to the security policy.

Every protected API request must independently validate identity, session, business access, property access and permissions.

Customers must only access their own records.

Employees must never access Owner-only information without explicit authorization.

Passport, QID, agreements, payment records and private documents must have restricted server-side access.

Test wrong passwords, expired tokens, revoked tokens, unrecognized devices, unauthorized API requests and cross-business data access.

Record actual test results and evidence. Never declare authentication secure without passing these tests.

